  "visualReview": "Chromium desktop and 320x640 settings: the two checked optional controls remain visibly checked and muted while disabled; enabling basic motion restores them.",
  "scope": "Nine final-build browser runs use the delivered MathJax 4.1.3 CDN configuration, with no local MathJax replacement. Motion checks cover all eight preference combinations and representative fractions, powers, ordinary clock and four font families. Full font geometry/structure/morph matrices were not rerun for this preference change. Audio tests use real browser oscillators and replay their commands through OfflineAudioContext; physical speaker listening was not repeated.",
  "autoplay": "Tests cover native autoplay policy and explicit pending/rejected resume fixtures. In these fresh browser contexts all three native startup attempts waited for interaction; each resumed on the first click with the saved gain and no restoration feedback.",
  "references": [
    "https://developer.chrome.com/blog/web-audio-autoplay",
    "https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/AudioContext/resume"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Initial probing found that a non-activation key on the focused sound button was incorrectly excluded from resumption; the handler now excludes only button activation events, and ignores untrusted events.",
    "The focused-button Space test was corrected to explicitly focus the button because WebKit on macOS does not focus it on click. No production change was required for that test correction.",
    "Earlier test-results/retained-motion-*, persisted-audio-signals-* and audio-preferences-* runs are preliminary; only saved-preferences-* runs are reported here."
